        "description": "<p>There will never be a leap second again. At least not for UTC.</p>\n<figure class=\"insert-image\"><img src=\"https://www.jeffgeerling.com/blog/2026/rejoice-the-utc-leap-second-is-dead/cgpm-resolution-5.jpg\"\n\t\t\talt=\"CGPM Resolution 5\" width=\"700\" height=\"auto\">\n</figure>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://www.bipm.org/en/cgpm-2026/resolution-5\">At the CGPM</a>, they decided the last leap second we'll ever see for UTC, or Coordinated Universal Time, happened back at the <a href=\"https://kb.meinbergglobal.com/kb/time_sync/leap_seconds/leap_second_announcement_2016\">end of 2016</a>.</p>\n<p>Of <em>course</em> they made that decision while I was out on vacation, so I'm just getting this video up now:</p>\n<div class=\"yt-embed\">\n <style>.embed-container { position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; } .embed-container iframe, .embed-container object, .embed-container embed { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }</style><div class='emb",
